Feature: GET financial_point_mapping

  ITAPPSIT-3268: Create API for Financial (Purple Box) Data

  GET /financial_point_mapping?{query_params}

  query_params:

  required query params:
  level_id
  level_type (only supporting level_type = registration initially)

  optional parameters:
  start_dttm_utc
  end_dttm_utc

  The test data is generated by the SQL script in FinancialPoints.sql.


  Background:
    Given I start with an empty context
    And I log in as a settlement API admin


  Scenario: Detailed validation of a single row

    When I call GET financial_point with the following parameters:
      | level_id       | 9999588e-6224-41b6-953d-72864e7d52eb |
      | level_type     | registration                         |
      | start_dttm_utc | 2023-01-01T00:00:00Z                 |
      | end_dttm_utc   | 2025-01-01T00:00:00Z                 |
    Then exactly 1 financial point mapping should be returned
    And the following financial point should be returned:
      | level_id             | 9999588e-6224-41b6-953d-72864e7d52eb |
      | level_type           | registration                         |
      | start_dttm_utc       | 2024-08-01T00:00:00.000Z             |
      | end_dttm_utc         | 2025-01-02T00:00:00.000Z             |
      | financial_point_id   | 5555588e-6224-41b6-953d-72864e7d52e1 |
      | channel_id           | 4010                                 |
      | financial_point_type | financial_point                      |
      | zone_id              | 111123ce-7379-4eac-af8e-c19d39d4b4a3 |


  Scenario: Return all rows for a registration

    * > Call with wide date range
    When I call GET financial_point with the following parameters:
      | level_id                  | 9999588e-6224-41b6-953d-72864e7d52eb        |
      | level_type             | registration         |
      | start_dttm_utc | 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z |
      | end_dttm_utc   | 4000-01-01T00:00:00Z |
    Then all financlal point mappings returned should match the query


  Scenario: No rows found because registration does not exist

    * > Call without date range
    Given I expect the next API call to return a status code of 404 and details of "Financial Point Mapping not found"
    When I call GET financial_point with the following parameters:
      | level_id      | <uuid>       |
      | level_type | registration |
    Then the expected status should be returned

    * > Call with wide date range
    Given I expect the next API call to return a status code of 404 and details of "Financial Point Mapping not found"
    When I call GET financial_point with the following parameters:
      | level_id                  | <uuid>               |
      | level_type             | registration         |
      | start_dttm_utc | 1980-01-01T00:00:00Z |
      | end_dttm_utc   | 3000-01-01T00:00:00Z |
    Then the expected status should be returned


  Scenario: Verify all conditionals around dates for a single row

    # only dev has the correct financial-point setup
    Given this scenario is only supported for the dev environment

    * > start_dttm_utc is inclusive and end_dttm_utc is exclusive of point's start time
    * > start_dttm_utc is exclusive of point's end time
    * > point start time = 2024-08-01
    * > point end time = 2025-01-02

    * > start_dttm_utc < point start time and end_dttm_utc < point start time (row not returned)
    Given I expect the next API call to return a status code of 404 and details of "Financial Point Mapping not found"
    When I call GET financial_point with the following parameters:
      | level_id                  | 9999588e-6224-41b6-953d-72864e7d52eb               |
      | level_type             | registration         |
      | start_dttm_utc | 2023-01-01T00:00:00Z |
      | end_dttm_utc   | 2024-07-31T00:00:00Z |
    Then the expected status should be returned

    * > start_dttm_utc < point start time and end_dttm_utc = point start time (row not returned)
    Given I expect the next API call to return a status code of 404 and details of "Financial Point Mapping not found"
    When I call GET financial_point with the following parameters:
      | level_id                  | 9999588e-6224-41b6-953d-72864e7d52eb               |
      | level_type             | registration         |
      | start_dttm_utc | 2023-01-01T00:00:00Z |
      | end_dttm_utc   | 2024-08-01T00:00:00Z |
    Then the expected status should be returned

    * > start_dttm_utc < point start time and end_dttm_utc > point start time and < point end time (row returned)
    When I call GET financial_point with the following parameters:
      | level_id                  | 9999588e-6224-41b6-953d-72864e7d52eb               |
      | level_type             | registration         |
      | start_dttm_utc | 2023-01-01T00:00:00Z |
      | end_dttm_utc   | 2025-01-01T00:00:00Z |
