  Scenario:   Validate default date parameters

    # only dev has the correct financial-point setup
    Given this scenario is only supported for the dev environment

    * > Call without date range (should return all rows for registration)
    When I call GET financial_point with the following parameters:
      | level_id      | 9999588e-6224-41b6-953d-72864e7d52eb       |
      | level_type | registration |
    Then exactly 3 financial point mappings should be returned
    And all financlal point mappings returned should match the query

    * > Only specify start date (end date defaults to 9999-01-01, should return subset of rows)
    When I call GET financial_point with the following parameters:
      | level_id      | 9999588e-6224-41b6-953d-72864e7d52eb       |
      | level_type | registration |
      | start_dttm_utc   | 2026-01-01T00:00:00Z |
    Then exactly 1 financial point mappings should be returned
    And all financlal point mappings returned should match the query

    * > Only specify end date (start date defaults to 1900-01-01, should return subset of rows)
    When I call GET financial_point with the following parameters:
      | level_id                  | 9999588e-6224-41b6-953d-72864e7d52eb               |
      | level_type             | registration         |
      | end_dttm_utc   | 2024-09-01T00:00:00Z |
    Then exactly 2 financial point mappings should be returned
    And all financlal point mappings returned should match the query


  Scenario: Query parameter errors

    * > end_dttm_utc is before start_dttm_utc
    Given I expect the next API call to return a status code of 400 and details of "start must be <= end"
    When I call GET financial_point with the following parameters:
      | level_id                  | <uuid>               |
      | level_type             | registration         |
      | start_dttm_utc | 2014-02-03T00:00:01Z |
      | end_dttm_utc   | 2014-02-03T00:00:00Z |
    Then the expected status should be returned

    * > cannot specify date before start of epoch
    Given I expect the next API call to return a status code of 400 and details of "Invalid start_dttm_utc, should be on or after 1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
    When I call GET financial_point with the following parameters:
      | level_id                  | <uuid>               |
      | level_type             | registration         |
      | start_dttm_utc | 1969-12-31T00:00:01Z |
      | end_dttm_utc   | 2014-02-03T00:00:00Z |
    Then the expected status should be returned

    * > invalid start_dttm_utc format
    Given I expect the next API call to return a status code of 400 and details of "The request failed validation"
    When I call GET financial_point with the following parameters:
      | level_id                  | <uuid>               |
      | level_type             | registration         |
      | start_dttm_utc | 1969-12-3100:00:01Z |
      | end_dttm_utc   | 2014-02-03T00:00:00Z |
    Then the expected status should be returned

    * > invalid end_dttm_utc format
    Given I expect the next API call to return a status code of 400 and details of "The request failed validation"
    When I call GET financial_point with the following parameters:
      | level_id                  | <uuid>               |
      | level_type             | registration         |
      | start_dttm_utc | 1969-12-31T00:00:01Z |
      | end_dttm_utc   | 2014-02-0300:00:00Z |
    Then the expected status should be returned

    * > level_id missing
    Given I expect the next API call to return a status code of 400 and details of "The request failed validation"
    When I call GET financial_point with the following parameters:
      | level_type | registration |
    Then the expected status should be returned

    * > level_type missing
    Given I expect the next API call to return a status code of 400 and details of "The request failed validation"
